## Scope

Current-main successor rooted in protected `main@b51f66add89755642c97deaa8acaeb2cc94a6bf4` without force-pushing or rewriting feature history.

This PR converges the token-ingress work into the existing production-copied and pre-catch-all registered `szl_budget_router.py` control plane rather than adding a parallel runtime package.

## Runtime implementation

The existing budget-tier endpoints and operator page are preserved. The same governed controller now adds:

- tokenizer-throughput and cache-locality routing;
- a digest-bound Semantic Token Contract covering tokenizer family, vocabulary, normalization, special tokens, added tokens, chat template, and document separator;
- exact representative-case qualification over token IDs and decoded text;
- a bounded, content-addressed Prefix Foundry bound to the semantic contract digest;
- deterministic file-native repository ingestion with containment, symlink refusal, file-count and byte budgets, binary classification, per-file SHA-256 rows, and a batch digest;
- verifier-budget reinvestment with explicit evidence authority;
- governed routes:
  - `GET /api/a11oy/v1/token-ingress/status`;
  - `POST /api/a11oy/v1/token-ingress/route`;
  - `POST /api/a11oy/v1/token-ingress/qualify`;
  - `POST /api/a11oy/v1/token-ingress/verification-budget`.

## Semantic admission law

A candidate tokenizer remains ineligible unless:

1. every semantic-component digest matches the declared oracle; and
2. every representative case has identical token IDs and identical decoded text.

Throughput, cache warmth, provider identity, and benchmark speed cannot override semantic mismatch.

## Public authority boundary

Public callers cannot:

- self-declare `MEASURED` tokenizer or cache telemetry;
- promote modeled savings to measured evidence;
- persist tokenized prefixes;
- read arbitrary repository files;
- invoke a provider or mutate a model;
- sign a record;
- mutate a database, deployment, or Hugging Face resource.

The public route set has zero provider, model, network, repository-read, persistent-prefix-write, signing, database, or deployment effectors.

## Deployment topology

This successor adds no Dockerfile COPY source and no second Hugging Face writer. It modifies the already managed `szl_budget_router.py` runtime file, which is already copied by the canonical image and registered by the established RESWEEP seam before both production catchalls.

The earlier parallel-module approach in #1327 was rejected by the protected Hugging Face candidate guard because it enlarged the managed runtime file set before canonical publication. This PR preserves that guard and removes the architectural collision instead of weakening admission.

## Verification

Added:

- focused budget/token-ingress core and HTTP tests;
- assembled-production-app route ownership and catchall-order tests;
- exact-candidate-head workflow using immutable action revisions and hash-locked Python dependencies;
- scoped whitespace rejection;
- a truth-labeled proof packet and rollback boundary.

Local source construction completed Python compilation and 13 focused tests. Hosted exact-head verification is pending.

## Honest non-claims

No live benchmark, tokenizer promotion, production traffic reroute, provider mutation, deployment, Hugging Face publication, measured latency/throughput/KV/energy/cost claim, or production readback is made by this PR.

## Rollback

Close this draft without merge, or revert the successor commits. Protected main and deployed provider state remain untouched until the normal protected path acts.

