## Current governance correction｜2026-08-25
This PR remains a **candidate Story & Board execution subroutine** for the existing Notion METHOD `MTH-DESIGN-PATTERN-LANGUAGE-001`. It is **not installed Current** and does **not** create a new Pattern/Architecture Skill, framework, gate system or project chapter.

Direct main readback confirms current `oleander-story-and-board` does not contain this explicit Pattern-network Integration Gate. Therefore the material delta is not absorbed, but it must remain subordinate to the existing Notion METHOD and current project authority.

## Reusable problem
Distributed rules can each be correct in isolation and still fail when composed:
- Route priority conflicts with optional reading;
- Brand language leaks into operational/safety semantics;
- Digital/game feedback becomes too dominant for landscape/body state;
- Physical support competes with experience instead of supporting it;
- Return priority is lost when many valid systems appear together.

The goal is **not** to produce another methodology diagram. It is to detect support/dependency/conflict relations before the final composition silently flattens them.

## Candidate sequence
`CURRENT AUTHORITY → EXISTING NOTION METHOD → BROKEN / INTENDED RELATION → CORE SPINE → SUPPORT PATTERNS → CONFLICTS → VARIANTS → SIDE-BY-SIDE READ → MEDIUM-SPECIFIC CRIT`.

The output may be a temporary relation map, review table or editable diagram during production. It does not automatically become a public-facing design artifact.

## Candidate conflict rules
- identify one core spine for the current object/journey/state;
- distinguish supporting patterns from co-primary systems;
- record explicit conflict winner when two valid rules cannot coexist at equal priority;
- preserve variants only when the decision context genuinely differs;
- read the composed result side by side with the strongest existing design;
- medium-specific visual/interaction critique remains required after the relation logic is correct.

`RELATION LOGIC PASS ≠ DESIGN PASS`.

## Existing-method / no-new-framework boundary
- Notion Pattern Language METHOD remains knowledge/method authority;
- Story & Board would only host an execution subroutine if promoted;
- do not create a separate Pattern Network database, skill owner, project axis or system gate;
- do not turn the training relation map into a permanent C04 public chapter merely because it is complete;
- use current Control Plane / Resolver / Artifact Review rather than adding another promotion gate.

## C04 trigger / current boundary
The original trigger remains materially understandable because C04 still contains distributed Route / optional reading / Digital / Physical / Brand / Return rules.

But current public C04 Web = PR #353, 18-section design-work reading + supplement. Any Pattern-network use should help resolve composition **inside current work**, not restart legacy dashboard/method pages or old pagination.

Persistent locks remain:
- ROUTE-03 authority unchanged;
- R06 frozen/no reopen;
- Return/service priority preserved;
- no new FIELD fact;
- no engineering or project Design promotion.

## Training provenance
The same six relations progressed:
- v1 REJECT: complete rule cards but no support/dependency/conflict visibility;
- v2–v4 REVISE: network logic improved but relation lines competed with first read;
- v5 KEEP FOR TRAINING: core spine + supports + contextual conflict winner with perimeter-routed support edges.

This is practice/failure knowledge, not a permanent project artifact or independent Design PASS.

## Promotion boundary
Before installation, validate the subroutine on another Current multi-system object or a materially different medium, prove that it reduces a real composition conflict without generating a parallel framework, then obtain independent review.

